From: gt510 <gt510@localhost>
Subject: msm8916: CPR open-loop voltages from the per-chip fuses

0113 runs CPR with "qcom,force-ceiling-voltage": every corner sits at its
ceiling, whatever the chip. MSM8916 fuses an open-loop voltage per fuse
corner (row 27), which downstream used as the starting point (and the only
voltage when CPR is off). Use it, without closed loop:

- cpr: complete msm8916_cpr_desc from the downstream msm8916-regulator.dtsi
  (init voltage = ref 1.05/1.15/1.375 V + 6-bit sign-magnitude x 10 mV,
  12-bit target quotients, ro-sel, step quotient 26, floors 1.05/1.05/
  1.1625 V, ceilings 1.05/1.15/1.375 V, no voltage interpolation);
  open_loop: never enable the closed loop and leave the CPR block off;
  no_quot_offset: MSM8916 has no quotient-offset fuses; optional
  "qcom,opp-max-microvolt" on a CPR OPP caps that level.
- qcom_spmi-regulator: set the linear step when only one range has set
  points; PM8916 S2 (ULT buck) reported none, so CPR's fuse parsing failed
  with -EINVAL.
- dts: row-27 nvmem cells, no force-ceiling, a fourth CPR level: 998.4 MHz
  in the TURBO fuse corner as downstream, capped at the TURBO floor 1.1625 V
  (its voltage since 0113); 1094.4 MHz and up at the TURBO fuse voltage;
  VDD_APC (S2) up to the downstream ceiling 1.375 V.

SM-T550 (kernel/cpr-fuses.py): row 27 = 0x988d920364911b29 → SVS 1.05 V,
NOM 1.11 V (→ 1.1125 V on the 12.5 mV regulator), TURBO 1.285 V
(→ 1.2875 V). So 200/400 MHz stay at 1.05 V, 533/800 MHz drop from 1.1625
to 1.1125 V, 998.4 MHz stays at 1.1625 V, 1094.4-1209.6 MHz drop from
1.35 to 1.2875 V.
